        "explanation": "The ATTENTION mechanism, introduced in the 2017 transformer architecture, is the key innovation. For each word, the model computes how strongly it should attend to every other word in the sequence, letting it gather relevant context from the whole sentence at once. This is how it resolves the reference of 'it' — a task that broke earlier systems. Hand-written rules (the rule-based era) were too brittle for such ambiguity; dictionary lookup is for translation, not reference; and simple co-occurrence counting (an n-gram-style statistic) lacks the contextual weighting attention provides.",
